							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">hmm. wow sorry to hear about what happened. but it does seem(from how you are describing this story) that you overreacted a little. im not sayin that you shouldnt be mad...but it didnt have to come out like that...also....<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=135.msg1745#msg1745">Quote from: hypknowledge* on October 19, 2006, 09:46:31 am</a></div><div class="quote"><br />and finally guy walks away and has the nerve to say: why you trippin?&#039;<br />im still mad so i say: you wann do somethin about it?&#039;<br />you can tell he was scared &#039;cause he said: &#039;did i say i wanted to?&quot; as he got down the stairs<br /><br />person in the background outside the classroom comes in and sits down: you need to calm down he already apologized.<br /><br />she also had the nerve to say i was tryin to start a fight in her school<br />i told em i didnt touch anybody and she said i was gettin loud [WHAT! IM FROM THE THIRD WORLD I GOTTA GET LOUD TO BE HEARD]<br /><br /></div><br /><br />.... if i was someone that happened to be there and witness what happened...i would think that you were trying to fight as well. sometimes everything isnt as complex and deeper than it seems....sometimes the things people say and do, like what the dude wrote about ur girl just comes out of pure stupidity. Build, educate, and listen. Acknowlege that they were wrong and stupid, use it to let them know whats up and to &#039;fight without fighting&#039;....before literally tryin to fight.<br /><br />again im sorry to hear wut happened...and i completely understand why u would be so pissed. dont take this the wrong way homie. im just lettin you know what im hearing and what im gettin out of this.</div>
