							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">from an outsiders point of view, It&#039;s one thing to stand up for your girl, but there is that point when you just have to back off.  He apoligized to her, now the ball is in her court, not yours.  Yes we give a woman our strength, but at times we need to let them flex their own muscles.  It wasn&#039;t a physical confrontation, only her pride and peace of mind were at stake.  And those battles for our peace of mind are the ones we fight on our own.<br /><br />You were right in defending her, but from what i&#039;ve gathered from your post, you hit the tipping point and kept going.  In doing so you elevated the situation beyond the point it needed to go. It&#039;s good that you got her back though.  Thick and thin right?<br /><br />Peace to you.</div>
